course: dictionary
lesson: 13479
title: Hysterical: upset, funny or out of control
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Hysterical» has three main meanings. The first is being so upset, frightened or excited that you cannot control your feelings. «The little boy was hysterical after he lost his mum in the shop.» Lost, crying and running about are the clues, so here it means out of control with fear.
explain: In everyday talk, people often use «hysterical» to mean extremely funny. «The film was hysterical!» The clues are that the friends are laughing and it is a film, so here it means very funny. This is informal, so it is fine in chat but less common in writing.
explain: The third meaning is laughing so much that you cannot stop. «We had hysterical laughter when the dog stole the sandwich.» Hysterical laughter means laughing that will not stop. To check any meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Hysterical» is an adjective. The adverb is «hysterically», and the noun «hysterics» is used in the phrase «in hysterics», which means laughing or crying out of control.
fact: «Hysterical» can mean so upset, frightened or excited that you cannot control your feelings.
fact: In informal speech, «hysterical» can mean extremely funny.
fact: «Hysterical laughter» means laughing so much that you cannot stop.
fact: In an emergency, try to stay calm and not get hysterical.
exercise: «The lost puppy was hysterical, screaming and running in circles.» What does hysterical mean here? | Extremely funny | Laughing so much you cannot stop | Calm and quiet | *So upset or frightened that you cannot control your feelings
exercise: Lily says, «The comedy show was hysterical!» What does she mean? | *Extremely funny | Very quiet | Very frightening | Very sad
exercise: «Everyone was in hysterics when the clown slipped on the banana peel.» What does «in hysterics» mean? | Crying quietly in fear | Standing very still | Sleeping soundly | *Laughing so much they could not stop
test: «The twins had hysterical laughter at the joke about the cat.» What does hysterical laughter mean? | *Laughing so much you cannot stop | Quiet, polite giggles | Crying with sadness | Loud shouting in anger
test: In a fire drill, the teacher says, «Stay calm and do not get hysterical.» What does she mean? | *Stay in control of your feelings and do not panic | Shout as loudly as you can | Dance around the room | Run back to get your bag
exam: «After the storm, Maya was so hysterical that she could not stop sobbing.» What does hysterical mean in this sentence? | Extremely funny | Laughing at a joke | Tired and sleepy | *Upset so much that she cannot control her feelings
